<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/victorian-home.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/victorian-home-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/victorian-home.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/new-hampshire-cities/">Cities</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Salem</span></nav><p class="kicker">Merrimack Valley · Rockingham County</p><h1>Salem, NH Insurance Appraiser</h1><p class="lede">Salem is a retail hub and a bedroom town at once, sitting on the state line to the south. We handle claim disputes for homeowners on quiet North Salem roads and for business owners along the busy corridors.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-light" href="/contact-nh-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="phero-chips"><li><small>County</small><b>Rockingham County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>Merrimack Valley</b></li><li><small>Housing</small><b>newer subdivisions, older lake cottages and commercial strip properties</b></li></ul></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="local-card"><div><h2 class="local-t">At a glance</h2><p><b>Areas we cover:</b> North Salem, the Canobie Lake area, Salem Depot, the Route 28 corridor.</p><p><b>Storm history:</b> The October 2011 “Snowtober” nor’easter loaded leafy trees with wet snow across southern Rockingham County, and Salem saw widespread limb damage to roofs, cars and power lines.</p></div><ul class="chips"><li>Snow on trees</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Microbursts</li><li>Burst pipes</li><li>Commercial roof leaks</li></ul></div>

<h2>Homes and storefronts in one town</h2>
<p>Salem is known for its shopping along Route 28 and I-93, but most of the town is residential. North Salem is quieter and more wooded, with older colonial-style homes and newer subdivisions. Around Canobie Lake, small cottages have been winterized and expanded over the decades. Salem Depot holds the town’s older center, and the redevelopment of the old racetrack site has added new housing, shops and offices in recent years.</p>
<h2>For homeowners: winter problems with long tails</h2>
<p>Ice dams are Salem’s most persistent residential claim. They form on almost any roof with poor attic ventilation, and they cause slow, hidden damage – wet insulation, staining, mold in wall cavities – that may not show up until spring. Insurers sometimes treat that damage as long-term leakage. Documenting when the ice built up, and when you first saw water, helps answer that.</p>
<h3>What a good ice-dam estimate includes</h3>
<ul>
<li>Removal and replacement of wet insulation, not just drywall.</li>
<li>Drying of framing and wall cavities, with moisture readings.</li>
<li>Interior paint and finish carried to a natural break, not a patch.</li>
<li>Roof edge repairs where the dam lifted shingles and flashing.</li>
</ul>
<p>Details in <a href="/nh-appraisal-services/ice-dam-roof-snow-appraisal/">ice-dam appraisal</a>.</p>
<h2>For business owners: bigger roofs, bigger gaps</h2>
<p>Salem’s commercial strip is full of low-slope roofs on retail buildings, restaurants and warehouses. Heavy snowpack, ponding water and summer hail all stress membrane roofs, and the arguments that follow can be expensive: full replacement or patching, the scope of wet insulation under the membrane, and business interruption while repairs happen. Commercial property policies usually include an appraisal clause, though the wording can differ from homeowners forms. Read more on <a href="/nh-appraisal-services/nh-commercial-hoa-appraisal/">commercial and HOA appraisal</a>.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Two policies, two clocks</b>Commercial and homeowners policies can carry different notice requirements and suit-limitation provisions. Check each policy and, if a deadline is close, ask a New Hampshire attorney.</div>
<h2>Lake cottages that became homes</h2>
<p>Converted cottages around Canobie Lake often have additions built in several phases, shallow foundations and plumbing run through unheated spaces. Frozen pipes and ice dams on low-pitch roofs are common. Estimating them well means understanding how each section was built.</p>
<p>Salem’s newer housing near the redeveloped racetrack site and in recent subdivisions brings its own questions. Builders often used specific siding and roofing lines that change or get discontinued within a few years. When a storm damages one elevation and the material can’t be matched, the argument shifts to how much of the house needs new material for a reasonable, uniform result. Policy wording on matching varies, so read yours closely.</p>
<h2>How New Hampshire Insurance Appraiser helps</h2>
<p>Whether it’s a house in North Salem or a storefront on Route 28, we review insurer estimates and, when appraisal is invoked, act as your appointed appraiser. We also serve as neutral umpires. Use the <a href="/nh-claim-calculators/percent-deductible-converter/">percent deductible converter</a> to see what your deductible means in dollars, or <a href="/contact-nh-appraiser/">contact us</a>.</p>

<h2>Appraisal help available in Salem</h2>
<p>Every New Hampshire Insurance Appraiser service is available in Salem and the surrounding towns, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/nh-appraisal-services/appraisal-clause-representation-nh/">Policyholder’s Appraiser on the Panel</a></li><li><a href="/nh-appraisal-services/homeowners-claim-appraisal-nh/">Single-Family Home Claims</a></li><li><a href="/nh-appraisal-services/nh-commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Condo, Association &amp; Business Claims</a></li><li><a href="/nh-appraisal-services/roof-and-hail-appraisal/">Roof Damage &amp; Hail Disputes</a></li><li><a href="/nh-appraisal-services/wind-microburst-tornado-appraisal/">Microburst &amp; Windstorm Losses</a></li><li><a href="/nh-appraisal-services/tropical-storm-hurricane-appraisal-nh/">Tropical Remnants &amp; Coastal Storms</a></li></ul>
<h2>Asked by Salem owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does a commercial policy have the same appraisal clause as a homeowners policy?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many commercial forms have a similar clause, but the wording varies. Read your policy’s appraisal section carefully before making a demand.</p></div></details><details><summary>I work across the state line. Does my Salem home’s claim follow New Hampshire practice?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. The policy on your Salem home and the property’s location are what matter. Ask a New Hampshire attorney about any legal questions.</p></div></details></div>
